review_comments.body:
Thanks for this. the diagnosis of #305 looks spot on, and the class-extension / category cases are clearly fixed. I also appreciate the focused tests around the reporter’s sample.

I checked the Codex note on lines 40–42 and agree with it. Entering _state_objc_declaration for every @protocol (and waiting only for @end) also catches forms that never have an @end, for example:

@protocol Foo;
@implementation Bar
- (void)doIt { }
@end

and file-scope uses like @protocol(NSObject). On this branch those cause later functions to be skipped entirely (I see [] instead of ["doIt"] / ["f"]); on master they are still found.

Could we only enter the skip-until-@end state for a real protocol definition, and leave forward declarations / @protocol(...) alone? A couple of regression tests for those cases would help lock it in.

Happy to take another look once that’s in. the @interface fix itself looks good; this is the main change I’d like before merging.
